Export TISSOT.h so board_config.h can include it.

board_config.h does `#include <pexpert/arm64/TISSOT.h>`, but that include
resolves against BUILD/obj/EXPORT_HDRS/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/, and a header
only lands there if it is listed in EXPORT_MD_LIST in this Makefile. Patch
0001 created TISSOT.h and added the include, but never added the file to the
export list, so the very first translation unit that pulls in board_config.h
died with:

    board_config.h:80:10: fatal error: 'pexpert/arm64/TISSOT.h' file not found

PRIVATE_KERNELFILES feeds both EXPORT_MD_LIST (headers used to compile xnu)
and INSTALL_KF_MD_LCL_LIST (Kernel.framework PrivateHeaders), so appending
TISSOT.h there fixes the build and installs the header in one place.

Logically part of 0001-add-tissot-board-config.patch; split into its own file
so trees that already applied 0001..0006 pick the fix up without re-applying
an altered 0001.

--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/Makefile
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/Makefile
@@ -16,7 +16,8 @@
 	boot.h \
 	H13.h \
 	VMAPPLE.h \
-	BCM2837.h
+	BCM2837.h \
+	TISSOT.h
 
 
 # Headers installed into System.framework/PrivateHeaders (userspace internal SDK only).
